; MM-RGN-3 at the RETURN (docs/memory-model-v2-design.md §2.3), and
; the one refusal that belongs to the signature alone.
;
;   1  `pick` answers its `@s` parameter as a `(String @r)`: AX3061.
;      Two named regions are UNORDERED, so `@s` is not known to
;      outlive `@r`.
;   2  `fresh` answers a value it allocated itself as `(String @r)`:
;      AX3061. The body allocates in its caller's current region
;      (MM-RGN-4), and a named region outlives that; allocating INTO
;      `@r` is stage S4's work, not this stage's.
;   3  `same` answers its own `@r` parameter: SILENT - the value the
;      signature promises.
;   4  `orphan` names `@q` on its result and on no parameter: AX3063
;      at the declaration. A region is chosen by the caller through an
;      argument, and a result-only region is one the callee would
;      have to invent - AX3040's shape, one type system over.
(import Str)

(:: pick (-> (String @s) (String @r) (String @r)))

(fn (pick a b) a)

(:: fresh (-> (String @r) (String @r)))

(fn (fresh a) (strConcat a "x"))

(:: same (-> (String @r) (String @r)))

(fn (same a) a)

(:: orphan (-> Int (String @q)))

(fn (orphan n) "x")

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
